## Grounding repair and the qualified cross-source proposal

The five state diagnostics exposed two restrictions in the existing native-definition witness: it accepted only flat nominal complements, and the encoder called it only for NOUN tokens. The repaired witness recognizes a complete state condition after *of* or *in which*. A verified native state genus with a complete condition noun can supply the identifying head when the gloss adds a qualifier, as in *arrest* followed by an interruption. Capitalized subjects require an explicit definition witness. A weaker nominal or type-thread match alone cannot select them. Outer copula negation, questions, uncertainty, alternatives and unrelated proper-name uses cannot supply this definition witness; independently supported noun grounding retains its own checks. Inner negation in an exact definition identifies its sense and supplies no bank value.

All five original diagnostics now select their intended native identities on the unchanged 018 dictionary. The three stored BE positives are emitted; the two reserved domains remain unknown. The earlier sentence and ambiguity suites have no regressions. A routing audit supplies complete definitions for all 425 native WordNet members of the broader state scope, both with a determiner and with capitalization. Its 850 cases identify 817 correctly and abstain on 33, including six token-boundary cases, with zero wrong identities or unsupported BE emissions. These are routing diagnostics, and their supplied definitions are part of the input. [Five-case rerun](019-state-grounding-diagnostic.json) · [State population audit](019-state-corpus-grounding.json)

The unadmitted parent *state of/in which* scope covers 952 records. Its 548 proposed additions include constructions whose genus still needs review. The narrower child requires *a/the state of being* followed by a lexical predicate. It reuses the existing source identity checks and native noun-frame machinery across WordNet and Wiktionary. Political state-of-place genera, bare *state of being*, existential *state of not being/existing*, dangling function words, alternate genera and multiple glosses are outside the child. The complete new population contains 460 Wiktionary definitions with 455 distinct glosses, all reviewed as qualified conditions, plus six WordNet records with five distinct glosses. The preview adds 466 BE positives and stages zero contradictions. [Parent preview](019-stative-parent-preview.json) · [Child preview](019-stative-being-preview.json)

The rule's warrant is the definition's own stative predication under the approved GSE convention. A separate SOMETHING assignment is not needed to state that condition; its absence remains unknown. The child assigns only BE. Whether the condition is actual, desired, possible, biological, or evaluative belongs to independently justified coordinates. The six planned withheld audits cover native inconceivability and unattainableness, Wiktionary unreality and annihilation, living as being alive, and boredom as being bored. Four separate release controls use employment, freedom, plurality as being plural, and the native state sense of senility. Full corpus replay, the existing benchmarks, the state routing audit, and semantic and runtime validation remain publication requirements.

