## Approved state-denotation convention

Rohan answered the pending question: “Yes—own state denotation is sufficient for BE=+1.” The approval explicitly includes well-arranged order and excludes a grammatical copula alone. It supplies the missing representation premise. The operational scope remains the reviewed exact native noun leaves with a qualified *state of being* genus. The new admission binds the explicit approval, scope, coordinate and warrant; the rule is foundational within that witnessed scope. Empirical admission continues to require model agreement. [Approved convention](019-approved-be-convention.json) · [Formal design](../../program/LEXICON_CONSTRUCTION_DESIGN.md#be-stative-content-scope)

The eight recorded held-out audits replay unchanged: four positive replies, three abstentions and the order zero. Care's earlier teaching abstention also remains unchanged. No new model question is needed to apply the convention. Care, order and the three temporary audit reservations now have a positive justification independent of those replies, so their bank domains may resolve without rewriting any historical model answer. The three original bare nonbeing/nonexistence/mixed-life controls remain outside scope and unresolved.

The foundational stage adds 466 BE positives across 460 Wiktionary and six WordNet records, with zero contradictions and no other-bank changes. It restores the three cases withheld by the provisional reservation stage because the approved sufficient condition now justifies them. The eight audits, nine construction questions, five separate calibration questions and one human representation decision remain separately counted. All 1,756 tests passed after convention admission and residual protocol 13 were added. Complete migration replay, sentence/runtime controls, the cumulative semantic checks and isolated publication replay remain required before activation. [Convention stage](019-convention-stage.json)

A constraint audit checked all 466 changed definitions on the frozen prior version. Their BE domains each contain all three signs, with no scope-matching prior BE constraint. The new rule is a foundational unary BE=+1 restriction. Conditional on migration reproducing the staged BE-only delta, this gives an exact support reduction of `3^466`, or 738.5925 bits, in the pinned per-definition bank-constraint model. It is not a posterior-entropy estimate or a measurement of geometric convergence across successive epochs. [Free-coordinate support proof](019-free-coordinate-support-proof.json)

The convention candidate completed full preflight and postflight replay: 401,596 records, complete search, zero mismatches and zero solver-limited components. Exact comparison reproduced all 466 staged changes, with no reopened or other-bank cells. The changes cover 460 spellings and 465 native sense groups. The 850-case grounding audit retained 817 correct identities and 33 abstentions, with zero wrong emissions and no regressions; the sentence and ambiguity benchmarks also passed. The support-factor proof therefore applies to the replayed delta. The subsequent isolated publication audit validated the same 401,596 records and identified all 109 cumulative semantic controls correctly, with zero wrong, conflicted, missing or abstained outcomes. Those controls include nine source/convention-derived BE expectations and are not independent linguistic gold. [Migration and benchmarks](019-verification.json) · [Prepublication checks](019-prepublication-validation.json) · [Contraction and count scopes](019-contraction.json) · [Publication](019-publication.json)

Release 019 activated with 408,627 assigned cells, 280,858 explicit zeros and 22,080,693 unresolved lexical cells. Its checksum equals the validated candidate exactly. A fresh default encoder loaded 019, compiled the five added convention controls and preserved the three out-of-scope unknown BE domains. The original care teaching abstention and order zero reply remain unchanged. The tested source and approval hashes still match. The one unchanged sentence-construction record is counted in replay and excluded from lexical progress. [Activation](sparse-release-019-activation.json) · [Published consumer](019-published-consumer-verification.json)

The rolling retention check keeps 019 and 018. Obsolete 017's source observations and definition identities match retained 018 exactly; its five retired-only metadata rows are preserved in a verified compressed audit archive. The duplicate candidate matches published 019 byte for byte. Both redundant databases were removed, unlinking 39,019,843,584 logical bytes. External backups were untouched; physical block reclamation was not measured. [Retention and audit witnesses](019-rollback-retention.json)


